What is here:
  data/maya_interpolation_modes_7500_binary.fbx
  data/maya_auto_clamp_7700_binary.fbx
  data/maya_tangent_spline_7700_binary.fbx
  data/maya_blend_shape_cube_7700_binary.fbx
      ufbx's test files: one animated cube each, written by Maya. The
      values Maya gives each curve at 24 frames a second are in ufbx's
      test/test_animation.h (the blend-shape cube's offsets and weights
      in test/test_skin.h) and, copied from there, in the tests in
      crates/shape-tools/src/fbx.rs.

What was read:
  ufbx.c, the reading of an AnimationCurve's keys (KeyAttrFlags,
  KeyAttrDataFloat, KeyAttrRefCount) and the evaluation of a curve. The
  rules crates/shape-tools/src/fbx.rs follows are ufbx's: which flag
  means what, the automatic tangent (the slope through the keys either
  side, its bias, its clamps), the TCB mix, the weights packed in a
  float's bits, and the cubic as a Bezier in time and value. The code
  is written anew in this project's structure.
